{
  "case_id": "2002-02-634",
  "document_hash": "77a3e8fe3a92be4e02a56c2b2d6b276cde47fafb95e8da92032bd36dda51eb15",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2002-02-634",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "77a3e8fe3a92be4e02a56c2b2d6b276cde47fafb95e8da92032bd36dda51eb15",
      "evidence_id": "ev-77a3e8fe3a92-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:10 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice O'Connor",
      "case_id": "2002-02-634",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "77a3e8fe3a92be4e02a56c2b2d6b276cde47fafb95e8da92032bd36dda51eb15",
      "evidence_id": "ev-77a3e8fe3a92-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: Well, Mr. Phillips, now, the contract presumably can be interpreted in accordance with the law of the State with jurisdiction."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2002-02-634",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "77a3e8fe3a92be4e02a56c2b2d6b276cde47fafb95e8da92032bd36dda51eb15",
      "evidence_id": "ev-77a3e8fe3a92-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "First in Volt and then again last term in Waffle House this Court made clear that, quote, arbitration under the Federal Arbitration Act is a matter of consent, not coercion."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Phillips",
      "case_id": "2002-02-634",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "77a3e8fe3a92be4e02a56c2b2d6b276cde47fafb95e8da92032bd36dda51eb15",
      "evidence_id": "ev-77a3e8fe3a92-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Because the question of whether the arbitrator has the authority to resolve the rights of unnamed third parties is not a question for the arbitrator to decide. That's a question for the court to decide."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice",
      "case_id": "2002-02-634",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "77a3e8fe3a92be4e02a56c2b2d6b276cde47fafb95e8da92032bd36dda51eb15",
      "evidence_id": "ev-77a3e8fe3a92-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: Why?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2002-02-634",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "77a3e8fe3a92be4e02a56c2b2d6b276cde47fafb95e8da92032bd36dda51eb15",
      "evidence_id": "ev-77a3e8fe3a92-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: What doctrine of state contract law led you -- led to this result, the doctrine of construe the instrument against, contra proferentem against the person who drafted it?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2002-02-634",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "77a3e8fe3a92be4e02a56c2b2d6b276cde47fafb95e8da92032bd36dda51eb15",
      "evidence_id": "ev-77a3e8fe3a92-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: Because?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Green Tree",
      "case_id": "2002-02-634",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "77a3e8fe3a92be4e02a56c2b2d6b276cde47fafb95e8da92032bd36dda51eb15",
      "evidence_id": "ev-77a3e8fe3a92-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Their own brief to the South Carolina Supreme Court repeatedly asserted that in Lackey the arbitrator, quote, took it upon himself to determine the propriety of a class-wide arbitration and certify a class."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2002-02-634",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "77a3e8fe3a92be4e02a56c2b2d6b276cde47fafb95e8da92032bd36dda51eb15",
      "evidence_id": "ev-77a3e8fe3a92-0002-0002",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the arbitrator in Bazzle made the arbitration award"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2002-02-634",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "77a3e8fe3a92be4e02a56c2b2d6b276cde47fafb95e8da92032bd36dda51eb15",
      "evidence_id": "ev-77a3e8fe3a92-0002-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The arbitrator said that he determined that a class action should proceed based on his careful review of the broadly drafted arbitration clause prepared by Green Tree."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Pillard",
      "case_id": "2002-02-634",
      "confidence": 0.85,
      "document_hash": "77a3e8fe3a92be4e02a56c2b2d6b276cde47fafb95e8da92032bd36dda51eb15",
      "evidence_id": "ev-77a3e8fe3a92-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Green Tree agrees that where an agreement authorizes it, class arbitration can be done, and so all they're asking you to do is to second-guess the State court's interpretation applying the rule of construction against the drafter, and I would very much dispute their characterization of what the South Carolina Supreme Court did of applying a -- a rule without any contractual or statutory directive to do so"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Unknown Justice",
      "case_id": "2002-02-634",
      "confidence": 0.5,
      "document_hash": "77a3e8fe3a92be4e02a56c2b2d6b276cde47fafb95e8da92032bd36dda51eb15",
      "evidence_id": "ev-77a3e8fe3a92-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "QUESTION: May I ask this, if you have another moment: Does this case have any real future significance, because isn't it fairly clear that all the arbitration agreements in the future will prohibit class actions?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Carter G. Phillips",
      "case_id": "2002-02-634",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "77a3e8fe3a92be4e02a56c2b2d6b276cde47fafb95e8da92032bd36dda51eb15",
      "evidence_id": "ev-77a3e8fe3a92-0003-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "we say point blank the arbitrator exceeded his authority to proceed as a class action, and that neither Green Tree nor any of the unnamed class members consented to have the arbitrator arbitrate their claims"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2002-02-634",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "77a3e8fe3a92be4e02a56c2b2d6b276cde47fafb95e8da92032bd36dda51eb15",
      "evidence_id": "ev-77a3e8fe3a92-0003-0003",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 59,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    }
  ],
  "schema_version": "1.0.0"
}
